WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.177
(curious instrumental music)

00:00:01.177 --> 00:00:03.609
- I've dedicated my life
to studying the ocean,

00:00:03.609 --> 00:00:07.016
but sometimes you come
across something so marvelous

00:00:07.016 --> 00:00:08.571
you have to wonder,

00:00:08.571 --> 00:00:11.195
"What the heck is going on down here?"

00:00:11.195 --> 00:00:13.870
Today we're talking
about the mimic octopus.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.953
- [Others] Mimic octopus.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.233
(curious instrumental music)

00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:24.641
- Octopuses are rather curious creatures.

00:00:24.641 --> 00:00:27.305
When exposed, they're
vulnerable to predators

00:00:27.305 --> 00:00:30.126
so typically, they like to stay hidden.

00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:31.902
When they do move they do so

00:00:31.902 --> 00:00:36.548
by walking along the ocean's
floor on their eight legs.

00:00:36.548 --> 00:00:39.803
(curious instrumental music)

00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:43.439
But in 1998, scientists
discovered an octopus

00:00:43.439 --> 00:00:46.051
residing in the shallow
waters of Indonesia

00:00:46.051 --> 00:00:48.551
doing something quite strange.

00:00:50.051 --> 00:00:51.994
Over the course of two years,

00:00:51.994 --> 00:00:55.354
they filmed it and nine
other similar octopuses

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:59.496
mimicking behaviors of at
least three different species.

00:00:59.496 --> 00:01:00.867
They found it swimming,

00:01:00.867 --> 00:01:03.777
its legs outstretched
high above the ocean floor

00:01:03.777 --> 00:01:05.232
like a lion fish,

00:01:05.232 --> 00:01:08.360
flattened out gliding over
the bottom like a flat fish,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.527
and extending its tentacles to
mimic a poisonous sea snake.

00:01:14.097 --> 00:01:18.288
This allows the mimic octopus
to hide in plain sight.

00:01:18.288 --> 00:01:19.288
Astonishing.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:25.153
(captivating instrumental music)

